&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on Ripple&#39;s Authentication and Authorization platform team, you&#39;ll help shape how identity works across our growing portfolio of payment, custody, and liquidity products. Our products have grown up using different identity providers and protocols, and we&#39;re now bringing them together into a unified, consistent experience — while also building the fine-grained authorization primitives that teams across Ripple rely on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW WE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI tooling is core to how our team works day-to-day — coding assistants, LLM-based workflows, and agentic tools across design, development, and operations. We&#39;re looking for people who already use these fluently, not just curious about them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction for Ripple&#39;s identity platform, including authentication flows, federation across multiple identity providers, and fine-grained authorisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of a unified identity experience across Ripple&#39;s product portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate platform services on Kubernetes, with a focus on reliability, observability, and secure secret management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with security, compliance, and product teams to translate regulatory requirements into platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear technical proposals and contribute to architecture discussions across the engineering org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on the team through code review, design feedback, and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
