&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend engineering experience in Golang or Java, including building and operating production applications within Kubernetes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or contributing to identity systems, ideally in a multi-tenant or federated context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI coding assistants and LLM-based tools as part of your day-to-day engineering workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating across teams and writing design documents that build alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern authentication protocols such as OAuth 2.0, OIDC, and SAML, and how they behave in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy-as-code approaches to authorization (attribute-based, relationship-based, or hybrid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
